# SFT execution status v0.77

2026-09-12. The fresh tiny-importer Linux CPU qualification harness and independent
supervisor are implemented and locally tested. This completes the local harness
preparation substep, not the native Linux qualification or Gate 5.

No actual checkpoint/trainer/tokenizer or dataset payload was opened. No AWS,
network, Docker, CI, GPU, inference, training, installation, instance action or
GitHub publication was initiated. Prior source and evidence remain unchanged.

## What is now connected

The fresh harness authenticates 57 code/control files (928,035 bytes), including
the unchanged 35-file importer closure. Host helper modules compile from the
authenticated in-memory bytes in private namespaces: stale bytecode or an
unverified filesystem module cannot replace those helper sources. The checkout
and host Python still require independent trust; this is not source immutability.

The accepted software archive is an already-local input, not downloaded by this
harness. Its fixed image is loaded, created, inspected and exported but never
started, pulled or rebuilt. Existing images are rejected before load. The
importer add-on uses its exact OwnedRootfs class; frozen installer rules are
unchanged. Only owned objects are retired, with no ambiguous-operation retry.

Three fixed cases run sequentially in fresh child processes: wrong entry pin,
wrong manifest pin, then positive tiny import. The negative worker must emit its
exact rejection and exit 1; the positive worker must pass the frozen full receipt.
Each case requires one bounded packet, EOF, exact exit status, descendant reaping
and empty owned-cgroup removal. A failed case stops the sequence.

The independent supervisor watches only the harness PID through a pidfd. It
never signals the guardian or a process group. Late exit cannot pass. SIGCHLD
must be default, any adopted child denies success, and stdout descriptor setup
failure still takes the owned cleanup path. The transport validator checks the
nested report bounds and false authority flags, not independent harness semantics.

The planned native limits are 900 seconds for the harness plus 120 seconds of
outer cleanup reserve; each case is at most 90 seconds, 4 GiB memory, no swap,
256 pids and two CPU cores of quota. These limits are implemented contracts, not
OS enforcement observations on this Mac. Guardian death, hostile root and
job-teardown cleanup remain outside the proof. The native commands were not run.

## Local verification and one test-launch correction

1,227 distinct targeted tests pass in the final configuration: 1,127 stdlib and
syscall-double tests on Python 3.11.15, 3.13.7 and 3.14.6, plus 100 generated
tiny-CPU tests on Python 3.13.7. There are 81 new tests. Each test subprocess has
an independent 60-second timeout. Ruff E,F,I,B,UP / py311 / line length 100 passes
on all six new Python files. This is not the full repository suite.

The extra CPU regression launch initially omitted HF_HUB_DISABLE_PROGRESS_BARS=1.
An optional HF-consumer compatibility test then created a tqdm monitor thread;
subsequent frozen single-owner guards correctly rejected that process (9 failures,
9 errors). A two-process, one-test diagnostic isolated this exact cause: the
monitor appears without the flag and does not appear with it. Restoring the
already-required worker environment yielded 100/100 passing tests in 2.866
seconds, 4.067 seconds supervised wall time. No guard, frozen test or importer
was weakened, and the failed test launch is recorded in the development report.
This was a local generated-fixture test correction, not a native attempt retry.

The new transaction tests use a fake daemon, real tiny generated tar extraction,
the genuine add-on and actual case receipt shapes. The independent supervisor
accepts those complete nested shapes. No native privilege, namespace, cgroup,
mount or guardian operation was exercised. Independent source review found no
remaining concrete blocker in the reviewed integration contracts.

The v0.76 report's 68 references (67 unique files), its report/verification/status,
all 57 source-admission bindings and the saved real-plan internal hash are checked.
Aggregate results and exact new bindings are in
`evidence/lumi-4b-sft-import-qualification-harness-v0.1.json`; separate structural
verification records two read-only passes.

